<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.4.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00907</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.4.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ccdfa7b6-f7f9-48ac-8e68-5307c03d56db</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="3b03d196-7526-4071-b198-999c2e4d4c08" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Match each equation with a verbal description that represents the same function.</para>
      <para>\(f(x)=2x+4\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct!  To get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para><para>The correct answer is to get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="234da651-94df-4ff5-af49-007f3ed47257" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(g(x)=2(x+4) \)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct!  To get the output, add 4 to the input, then multiply the result by 2.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para><para>The correct answer is To get the output, add 4 to the input, then multiply the result by 2<emphasis>.</emphasis>  </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="bf984679-4679-4e9b-bd3b-85ae0fd95e57" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(h(x)=4x+2\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct!  To get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para><para>The correct answer is to get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="5955ed6d-6f72-4398-bb5d-80cb2b9881a9" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(k(x)=4(x+2)\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct!  To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para><para>The correct answer is To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="0d08ce71-3fc2-4a8f-a27e-c97d363f1731" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Functions \(A\) and \(B\) are defined by these equations.
          \(A(x)=25+10x\) \(B(x)=80-15x\) 
          Which function has a greater value when \(x\) is 2.5? </para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(A(x)=25+10x\)</para><para>\(B(x)=80-15x\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!  Function A has a greater value because B(2.5)=42.5 and A(2.5)=50.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.3. </para><para>The correct answer is Function A has a greater value because \(B(2.5)=42.5\) and \(A(2.5)=50\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="998043ad-68ac-4dc6-b932-88437166f755" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which function is greater when \(x = 4\)? </para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(f(x)=2x-7\)</para><para>\(f(x)=-3x+1\)</para><para>\(f(x)= -5x+2\)</para><para>\(f(x)=x-10\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(f(x)=2x -7\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para><para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=2x -7\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="a6cbad77-b6a6-46d6-9940-8b2019b175a9" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which function rule describes the table below: </para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <tgroup cols="6"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              \(x\)
            </emphasis></entry><entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5
            </entry>
            <entry>
              6
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              \(y\)
            </emphasis></entry><entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5
            </entry>
            <entry>
              7
            </entry>
            <entry>
              9
            </entry>
            <entry>
              11
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
    <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(f(x)=x+1\)</para><para>\(f(x)=3x-3\)</para><para>\(f(x)=2x-1\)</para><para>\(f(x)=x+2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(f(x)=2x-1\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=2x-1\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="5ea74f7e-7211-4aa4-ae4f-db4b69b5ad08" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Write a function \(g(x)\) for the following statement: to get the output, subtract 4 from the input, then multiply the result by 2.</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(g(x)=2x-4\)</para><para>\(g(x)=-4-2x\)</para><para>\(g(x)=x -8\)</para><para>\(g(x)=2(x-4)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(g(x)=2(x-4)\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.1. </para><para>The correct answer is \(g(x)=2(x-4)\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="ad08a7ed-c590-4281-852d-11570c6bce38" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Write a function \(h(x)\) for the following statement: to get the output, multiply the input by 5 and then add 2.</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(h(x)=5(x+2)\)</para><para>\(h(x)=5x+2\)</para><para>\(h(x)=x +2(5)\)</para><para>\(h(x)=x+2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(h(x)=5x+2\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.1.</para><para>The correct answer is \(h(x)=5x+2\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="c60f5cda-248c-45f1-b8d8-19fc43601821" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Find the value of \(f(x)=−2x−3\) when \(x=2\).</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>7</para><para>1</para><para>-1</para><para>-7</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! -7</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para><para>The correct answer is -7. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="e067d2ce-4e9a-4fe3-87c3-6fbb16068c95" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Examine the table below. Find \(g(2.5)\) using the rule for this table. </para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <tgroup cols="5"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              \(x\)
            </emphasis></entry><entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              \(g(x)\)
            </emphasis></entry><entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              6
            </entry>
            <entry>
              10
            </entry>
            <entry>
              14
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
    </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(g(x)=4x-2\), \(g(2.5)=8\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.4.</para><para>The correct answer is \(g(x)=4x-2\), \(g(2.5)=8\). </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
